		<title type="html"><![CDATA[maxVelocity in setJointMotorControlArray]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=43088#p43088"><![CDATA[
There doesn't seem to be a way to set the <strong class="text-strong">maxVelocity</strong> (or in this case <strong class="text-strong">maxVelocities</strong>) for joints in <strong class="text-strong">setJointMotorControlArray</strong> like you can in <strong class="text-strong">setJointMotorControl2</strong>. Is there a reason for this and maybe a workaround?<br>In my benchmarks <strong class="text-strong">setJointMotorControlArray</strong> is about 15% faster than calling <strong class="text-strong">setJointMotorControl2</strong> for each of the 18 actuators, which helps as I am running a large number of simulations.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=13757">chrismailer</a> — Sat Aug 29, 2020 8:51 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
